      "text/markdown": [
       "### The YRF Spy Universe: Because One Middle-Aged Hero Isn’t Enough\n",
       "\n",
       "Welcome to the **YRF Spy Universe**, India’s answer to the MCU, but with 200% more hair gel and mandatory dance breaks. Produced by Yash Raj Films, this franchise is a collection of \"interconnected\" movies starring Bollywood’s most expensive aging men—Salman Khan (**Tiger**), Shah Rukh Khan (**Pathaan**), and Hrithik Roshan (**Kabir**)—who spend their time saving India from bioweapons while looking fabulous in tactical scarves.\n",
       "\n",
       "#### The \"Strategic\" Timeline\n",
       "The universe technically started in 2012 with *Ek Tha Tiger*, though producer Aditya Chopra didn't realize he was making a \"universe\" until *Pathaan* (2023) made enough money to buy a small country. The solution? Just retrofit the old movies together like a child forcing two different Lego sets to fit. \n",
       "\n",
       "**The Current Roster:**\n",
       "*   **The Tiger Series:** Salman Khan falls for a Pakistani spy (Zoya) because apparently, romance is the best way to handle cross-border tensions. \n",
       "*   **War:** Hrithik Roshan plays a rogue agent who isn't actually rogue. It features a plot twist involving plastic surgery that would make a soap opera writer blush.\n",
       "*   **Pathaan:** Shah Rukh Khan returns to save the world from John Abraham (a very buff terrorist) and rescues Tiger from a Russian prison because bros don't let bros stay incarcerated.\n",
       "\n",
       "#### What’s Next?\n",
       "Coming soon is *War 2* and *Alpha*, the latter finally letting a woman (**Alia Bhatt**) lead the franchise—presumably to prove that women can also look intense while ignoring the laws of physics. If you enjoy musical numbers in the middle of a terrorist manhunt, you’ve found your cinematic peak."
      ],
